## Subcommand behavior

- **inject** (default): walk all targets → exact-substring check → insert missing tags immediately before `</body>` with single-`\n` separator → exit 0 on success, 1 on r/w error.
- **drift-check**: walk all targets → count expected vs present → exit 0 if all OK, 1 if any missing, 2 on read error.
- **undo**: walk all targets → remove any line containing one of the 3 known tag substrings → collapse `\n{3,}` → `\n\n` for clean restoration → exit 0 on success, 1 on r/w error.

## Idempotency contract

Per-tag: if exact substring `<script defer src="...read-tracker.js">` exists, that single tag is skipped (and same independently for essay-typing). Re-running `inject` on a fully-injected tree makes 0 writes and 365 `SKIP` log lines.

## Run sequence (this session)

1. `inject` → 363 modified (article HTML) + 2 skipped (index already had tag from previous run) → exit 0
2. `inject` (re-run) → 0 modified, 365 skipped → exit 0 (idempotent)
3. `drift-check` → 365/365 OK → exit 0
4. `undo` → 365 modified (all tag lines removed) → exit 0
5. `drift-check` → 365 MISSING → exit 1
6. `inject` (final restore) → 365 modified → exit 0
7. `drift-check` → 365/365 OK → exit 0

Final state: all 365 files contain the expected tags.

